# Versioning

VirtFoundry uses **Semantic Versioning 2.0.0** while pre-1.0 (`0.x.y`).

## Repositories (release together)

| Repo | Version location | Git tag | Published artifact |
|------|------------------|---------|-------------------|
| [core](https://github.com/virtfoundry/core) | git tag `vX.Y.Z` | `v0.2.0` | GHCR `core`, `ui` |
| [helm-charts](https://github.com/virtfoundry/helm-charts) | `Chart.yaml` `version` + `appVersion` | `v0.2.0` | Helm repo on GitHub Pages |

**Rule:** For a user-facing release, bump **both** repos to the **same** `X.Y.Z` and use the **same** git tag `vX.Y.Z`.

## SemVer (pre-1.0)

| Bump | When | Examples |
|------|------|----------|
| **PATCH** `0.1.0 → 0.1.1` | Bug fixes, doc-only chart fixes | NAD typo, UI label |
| **MINOR** `0.1.0 → 0.2.0` | New features, chart profile changes | VM templates, public network fix |
| **MAJOR** `0.x → 1.0.0` | First stable API/chart contract | Reserved for 1.0 launch |

Breaking changes before 1.0 may land in MINOR releases; document them in `CHANGELOG.md`.

## Release checklist

1. Update `CHANGELOG.md` in **both** repos
2. Chart: bump `charts/virtfoundry/Chart.yaml` (`version` + `appVersion`)
3. Chart: bump default `images.*` tags in `values.yaml` to match release
4. Merge to `main` (PR + cluster validation when applicable)
5. Tag and push: `git tag vX.Y.Z && git push origin vX.Y.Z` in **both** repos
6. CI publishes GHCR images (app) and Helm package (chart)
7. Docs site rebuilds on tag push (MkDocs → GitHub Pages `/docs/`)

## Branch → artifact mapping

- `main` → `latest` images, chart lint CI
- `vX.Y.Z` tag → semver images (`0.2.0`, `0.2`), Helm `index.yaml` entry

Do **not** tag from feature branches except release candidates (`v0.2.0-rc.1` optional).
